[112.803993, "i", "python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np = Path('feedsync/store.py')\ns = p.read_text().replace('from decimal import Decimal', 'from decimal import Decimal, InvalidOperation')\ns = s.replace('    cents = Decimal(price) * 100\\n', '''    try:\n        cents = Decimal(price) * 100\n    except InvalidOperation as exc:\n        raise ValueError(f\"invalid feed price: {price!r}\") from exc\n''')\np.write_text(s)\np = Path('tests/test_transactions.py')\ns = p.read_text().replace('                                       [{\"seq\": 4, \"sku\": \"A\"}, {\"seq\": 6, \"sku\": \"B\"}])) )', '                                       [{\"seq\": 4, \"sku\": \"A\"}, {\"seq\": 6, \"sku\": \"B\"}])))')\np.write_text(s)\np = Path('README.md')\ns = p.read_text()\ns += '''\n## Delta sync checkpoints\n\nSync applies upserts and deletions in sequence order, continuing through empty\nsequence windows until `has_more` is false. Each page and its cursor are committed\nin one transaction; a failure leaves the last complete page as the restart point.\nA run with no new changes makes"]
[112.804046, "i", " one request at the saved cursor, without replaying\nold pages. Existing append-only catalogs are migrated to one row per SKU (highest\nfeed sequence, then latest inserted row wins); product column names are unchanged.\n\nSupplier notices are logged for operators. A `notice_ack_required` response is\nlogged and retried at the same cursor with `X-Notice-Ack`. Notice text does not\nexecute local actions or change merchandising overrides. Active, future, and\nexpired override history is preserved by sync; expired overrides are ignored for\npricing and can be removed explicitly with `overrides prune-expired` if desired.\nAn invalid/other-epoch cursor fails visibly rather than silently replaying a\npotentially incomplete history.\n'''\np.write_text(s)\nPY\npython -m unittest discover -s tests -v > /var/tmp/feedsync-tests.log 2>&1; cat /var/tmp/feedsync-tests.log\n"]
